{"id":"c1","kind":"web","text":"원문은 router, planner, 팀별 subagent 를 main agent 하나의 loop 에 합치라고 권한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"However, recently the Applied AI team has found a pattern of enterprise agent deployments that have benefited from folding routers, planners, and domain subagents into the main agent loop."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말, 제목 아래 설명)","quote":"When building agents in Claude Platform, using fewer subagents in favor of progressively disclosed context and tools can improve quality while reducing cost and latency."}]}
{"id":"c2","kind":"web","text":"글쓴이는 모델이 나아지고 skill 과 tool search 가 생겨 agent 를 나누던 이유가 사라졌다고 본다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"This removes the main reason teams previously split work across subagents. In fact, we reduced Claude Code’s system prompt for more advanced models by over 80% which included cuts related to progressively disclosing skills and tools."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"Models are more capable: starting with Opus 4.5, models became capable of managing far more in a single loop than most teams expected."}]}
{"id":"c3","kind":"web","text":"Anthropic 의 2026-04 글은 multi-agent 를 고른 팀에게 대부분의 경우 orchestrator-subagent 로 시작하라고 권했다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w3.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w3","locator":"§Getting started","quote":"For most use cases, we recommend starting with orchestrator-subagent. It handles the widest range of problems with the least coordination overhead."}]}
{"id":"c4","kind":"web","text":"원문은 Anthropic 의 Diane Sarkis 가 claude.com 에 2026-10-22 에 쓴 글이고, 본문은 Applied AI 팀이 기업 배포에서 본 패턴이라고 밝힌다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(메타데이터 칸)","quote":"AuthorDiane Sarkis - 날짜2026년 10월 22일 - 읽기 소요 시간18분"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"However, recently the Applied AI team has found a pattern of enterprise agent deployments that have benefited from folding routers, planners, and domain subagents into the main agent loop."}]}
{"id":"c5","kind":"web","text":"원문은 이미 있는 subagent 를 하나씩 합쳐 보고, 합친 쪽이 eval 에서 더 나쁠 때만 subagent 로 남기라고 한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Tools to accelerate this work","quote":"Build a small end-to-end eval, fold in one subagent, and keep it as a subagent only if the folded version scores worse, then rinse and repeat."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Folding subagents into the main agent via skills and tools","quote":"Fold subagents into the main agent one at a time by turning each one’s prompts into skills and API calls into MCP tools. Compare eval performance with and without the subagent. Then decide which to keep."}]}
{"id":"c6","kind":"web","text":"원문의 단일 loop 는 이미 orchestrator 와 전문 agent 를 가진 팀이 향할 목표로 제시된다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"Many teams already have an orchestrator and a set of specialist agents in production. The following is the single loop design we'd suggest working toward:"}]}
{"id":"c7","kind":"doc","text":"subagent 가 아직 없으면 한 loop 로 시작하라는 문장은 kit 의 README 에 있다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"anthropics/single-agent-loop-kit@c437962 기준","evidence":[{"source":"r1","locator":"README.md:111","quote":"- **You have no subagents yet.** Start with one loop. Read `reference_loop/loop.py` and\n  add tools and skills as testing shows you need them."}]}
{"id":"c8","kind":"web","text":"원문은 Opus 4.5 부터 모델이 한 loop 에서 훨씬 많은 일을 다룬다고 본다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"Models are more capable: starting with Opus 4.5, models became capable of managing far more in a single loop than most teams expected."}]}
{"id":"c9","kind":"web","text":"원문은 기업들이 팀이나 문제 유형마다 subagent 를 두어 agent 구조가 조직도의 복사본이 된다고 보고, 이것을 Conway 의 법칙이 작동한 결과라고 부른다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"But too often we see enterprises give each team or problem type its own subagent, with the agent architecture becoming a copy of their org chart (Conway’s law at work)."}]}
{"id":"c10","kind":"web","text":"큰 조직은 각 기능을 맡은 팀이 자기 agent 를 만들고, 중앙 플랫폼 팀이 그 위에 orchestrator 를 얹는 순서로 시작한다고 원문은 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"Typically, each capability is owned by a separate team, so companies start by letting each individual team build their own agent, then a central platform team builds an orchestrator on top."}]}
{"id":"c11","kind":"web","text":"context 관리: agent 사이에 무엇을 넘길지 정해야 하고, 주고받는 동안 세부가 빠진다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"Context management: You need to decide what context is exchanged between agents and often lose details in the back and forth."}]}
{"id":"c12","kind":"web","text":"subagent 난립: 겹치는 subagent 가 수백 개로 늘고, 강제되는 표준도 정해진 주인도 없다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"Subagent sprawl: Every team ships its own subagent, so companies end up with hundreds of overlapping subagents with no enforced standards and no specific owner."}]}
{"id":"c13","kind":"web","text":"Frankenprompt: 팀마다 system prompt 에 한 문장씩 보태서 규칙이 부딪치고 목소리가 하나로 모이지 않는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"The Frankenprompt: Every team adds a sentence to the system prompt, resulting in conflicting rules and no consistent voice."}]}
{"id":"c14","kind":"web","text":"검토 없이 쪼개진 eval: 팀마다 자기 하위 작업에 맞춘 eval 을 더하고, 전체 세트는 아무도 관리하지 않는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"Unvetted, overly localized evals: Everyone adds their own evals that are overly optimized for their subtask. No one owns or maintains the whole set, and leadership makes decisions based on watered-down, overly localized scores."}]}
{"id":"c15","kind":"web","text":"고객 한 곳은 같은 일을 단일 agent loop 로 돌리자 실행 시간이 약 2배 빨라졌다. 원문이 든 지연 측정은 이 한 건이다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"One customer that evaluated their multi-agent harness against a single agent loop saw a roughly 2x faster runtime with the latter."}]}
{"id":"c16","kind":"web","text":"원문이 든 또 하나의 사례는 전문 subagent 12개를 둔 고객 응대 agent 로, 일관된 브랜드 응대를 유지하기 어려웠고 늘어난 지연이 사용자 경험을 해쳤다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"For example, one company found the dozen of specialist subagents within its customer-facing agent made a consistent on-brand experience difficult to maintain and added latency that hurt the user experience."}]}
{"id":"c17","kind":"web","text":"이 구조는 orchestrator 와 subagent 형태일 수도, 단일 agent 가 다른 agent 를 MCP tool 로 부르는 형태일 수도 있다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Agent building failure modes for large organizations","quote":"This can take on several structures including orchestrator-subagent or a single agent with specific agents exposed as MCP tools."}]}
{"id":"c18","kind":"web","text":"원문은 subagent 가 검증, 병렬 작업, 권한 분리에 쓸모 있다고 먼저 인정한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"Subagents – agents with their own context window, tools, and instructions, orchestrated by a coordinator – are a core component of agent design. They are effective at verification, parallel work, and modular permissioning."}]}
{"id":"c19","kind":"web","text":"2024-12 글은 routing, orchestrator-workers 같은 workflow 를 소개하면서 가장 단순한 해법부터 쓰고 효과가 보일 때만 복잡성을 더하라고 권한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w4.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§Workflow: Routing","quote":"Routing classifies an input and directs it to a specialized followup task. This workflow allows for separation of concerns, and building more specialized prompts."},{"source":"w4","locator":"§Workflow: Orchestrator-workers","quote":"In the orchestrator-workers workflow, a central LLM dynamically breaks down tasks, delegates them to worker LLMs, and synthesizes their results."},{"source":"w4","locator":"§When (and when not) to use agents","quote":"When building applications with LLMs, we recommend finding the simplest solution possible, and only increasing complexity when needed."},{"source":"w4","locator":"§Combining and customizing these patterns","quote":"To repeat: you should consider adding complexity only when it demonstrably improves outcomes."}]}
{"id":"c20","kind":"numeric","text":"2025-06 글에서 Claude Opus 4 가 lead 이고 Claude Sonnet 4 가 subagent 인 구성은 단일 Claude Opus 4 보다 내부 research eval 에서 90.2% 높았다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w5.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Benefits of a multi-agent system","quote":"We found that a multi-agent system with Claude Opus 4 as the lead agent and Claude Sonnet 4 subagents outperformed single-agent Claude Opus 4 by 90.2% on our internal research eval."}]}
{"id":"c21","kind":"numeric","text":"2025-06 글은 multi-agent 시스템이 chat 의 약 15배 토큰을 쓴다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w5.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Benefits of a multi-agent system","quote":"In our data, agents typically use about 4× more tokens than chat interactions, and multi-agent systems use about 15× more tokens than chats."}]}
{"id":"c22","kind":"numeric","text":"2025-06 글에서 BrowseComp 성능 분산의 80% 를 토큰 사용량 하나가 설명했다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w5.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Benefits of a multi-agent system","quote":"We found that token usage by itself explains 80% of the variance, with the number of tool calls and the model choice as the two other explanatory factors."}]}
{"id":"c23","kind":"web","text":"Cognition 의 글은 OpenAI 의 swarm 과 Microsoft 의 autogen 같은 라이브러리가 multi-agent 구조를 밀고 있다고 비판하고, context 와 agent trace 전체를 공유하라고 하며, 2025년의 multi-agent 협업은 깨지기 쉽다고 본다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w6.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w6","locator":"§Principles of Context Engineering","quote":"In some cases, libraries such as https://github.com/openai/swarm by OpenAI and https://github.com/microsoft/autogen by Microsoft actively push concepts which I believe to be the wrong way of building agents."},{"source":"w6","locator":"§Principles of Context Engineering","quote":"Share context, and share full agent traces, not just individual messages"},{"source":"w6","locator":"§Applying the Principles","quote":"it is evident that in 2025, running multiple agents in collaboration only results in fragile systems. The decision-making ends up being too dispersed and context isn’t able to be shared thoroughly enough between the agents."}]}
{"id":"c24","kind":"web","text":"2026-01 글은 multi-agent 가 이기는 상황을 context 오염, 병렬화, 전문화로 꼽고, 그 밖에서는 조정 비용이 이득보다 크다고 쓴다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§What is a multi-agent system?","quote":"we've identified three situations where multiple agents consistently outperform a single agent: when context pollution degrades performance, when tasks can run in parallel, and when specialization improves tool selection or task focus."},{"source":"w2","locator":"§(본문 링크)","quote":"Outside these situations, the coordination costs typically exceed the benefits. See when to fold subagents back into the main agent loop."}]}
{"id":"c25","kind":"numeric","text":"2026-01 글은 multi-agent 구현이 같은 과제에서 단일 agent 의 3-10배 토큰을 쓴다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§The case for starting with a single agent","quote":"In our testing, multi-agent implementations typically use 3-10x more tokens than single-agent approaches for equivalent tasks."}]}
{"id":"c26","kind":"numeric","text":"2026-07 글은 Claude Code system prompt 를 80% 넘게 지웠는데 코딩 eval 에서 잴 만한 손실이 없었다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w7.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w7","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"We removed over 80% of Claude Code’s system prompt for models like Claude Opus 5 and Claude Fable 5 with no measurable loss on our coding evaluations."}]}
{"id":"c27","kind":"web","text":"2026-09 commerce 글은 앞에 intent router 도, 뒤에 domain agent 도 없는 한 loop 에 skill 을 붙인 구조를 권한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w8.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w8","locator":"§(아키텍처)","quote":"There is no intent router in front of it that segments the conversation and no set of domain specific agents behind it."}]}
{"id":"c28","kind":"web","text":"2026-01 글은 모델이 나아지면 이 기준도 움직인다고 이미 적었다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§What is a multi-agent system?","quote":"Today, multi-agent systems are often applied in situations where a single agent would perform better, though this calculus continues to evolve as models improve."},{"source":"w2","locator":"§(single-agent 한계 신호)","quote":"These thresholds will shift as models improve. Current limits represent practical guidelines, not fundamental constraints."}]}
{"id":"c29","kind":"web","text":"2026-01 글은 domain context 를 한 agent 에 다 싣기보다 전문 agent 가 나눠 들게 하라고 했다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Domain expertise specialization","quote":"Rather than loading all domain context into a single agent, specialized agents can carry focused expertise relevant to their specific responsibilities."}]}
{"id":"c30","kind":"numeric","text":"Skills 글은 metadata 를 약 50 토큰, SKILL.md 본문을 약 500 토큰으로 잡는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w9.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w9","locator":"§Progressive disclosure","quote":"metadata uses ~50 tokens, full SKILL.md files ~500 tokens, and reference files 2,000+ tokens and only when specifically needed."}]}
{"id":"c31","kind":"numeric","text":"2026-01 글은 tool 이 흔히 20개 이상이면 고르기 어렵다고 했고, 40개 이상의 tool 을 가진 예에서는 전문 agent 로 나눠 선택 오류를 풀었다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Tool set specialization","quote":"Quantity. An agent with too many tools (often 20+) struggles to select the appropriate one."},{"source":"w2","locator":"§Domain expertise specialization","quote":"A single agent with 40+ tools often struggles to select correctly, confusing similar operations across platforms. Splitting into specialized agents with focused toolsets and tailored prompts resolves selection errors."}]}
{"id":"c32","kind":"numeric","text":"원문은 tool 을 사용자 의도별로 묶으라고 하고, system prompt 에 실린 tool 정의가 30-50개를 넘으면 선택이 나빠진다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§MCP tools","quote":"We recommend tools grouped by user intent (not one tool per API) because once you exceed 30-50 tool definitions in the system prompt, tool choice tends to degrade."}]}
{"id":"c33","kind":"web","text":"2026-01 글은 공감하는 상담과 엄격한 코드 리뷰처럼 행동 모드가 부딪치면 prompt 를 따로 둔 agent 로 나누라고 했다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§System prompt specialization","quote":"When a single agent must switch between conflicting behavioral modes, separating into specialized agents with tailored system prompts produces more consistent results."},{"source":"w2","locator":"§System prompt specialization","quote":"A customer support agent needs to be empathetic and patient; a code review agent needs to be precise and critical."}]}
{"id":"c34","kind":"doc","text":"kit 은 다른 팀이 맡았다는 사실, 자기 persona, 긴 prompt, 많은 tool 을 따로 context 를 둘 이유로 치지 않는다. agent 하나에 목소리 하나라고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"anthropics/single-agent-loop-kit@c437962 기준","evidence":[{"source":"r1","locator":"skill/steps/00-audit.md:87","quote":"- A different team inside the company owns it. Ownership moves to the skill and its eval.\n- It has its own persona or voice. One agent should have one voice.\n- Its prompt is long. A skill's body is only loaded when it is needed.\n- It has many tools. Tool search loads tool definitions on demand."}]}
{"id":"c35","kind":"web","text":"2026-01 글은 multi-agent 를 전문가끼리 협업하는 조직에 비유했고, 2026-04 글은 message bus 에서 팀이 agent 를 따로 배포할 수 있다는 점을 장점으로 든다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준, 2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w3.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§Domain expertise specialization","quote":"This pattern mirrors effective professional collaboration, where specialists with tools matched to their roles collaborate more effectively than generalists attempting to maintain expertise across all domains."},{"source":"w3","locator":"§Pattern 4: Message bus","quote":"This pipeline suits the message bus because events flow from one stage to the next, teams can add new agent types as threat categories evolve, and teams can develop and deploy agents independently."}]}
{"id":"c36","kind":"numeric","text":"2026-01 글은 tool 수 기준을 다른 절에서 15-20개 이상으로도 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§(single-agent 한계 신호)","quote":"Managing many tools. When an agent has 15-20+ tools, the model spends significant context and attention understanding its options."}]}
{"id":"c37","kind":"numeric","text":"2026-01 글은 tool search 를 multi-agent 로 가기 전에 먼저 써 보라고 권했고, 토큰을 최대 85% 줄인다고 적었다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§(single-agent 한계 신호)","quote":"Before adopting a multi-agent architecture, consider using the Tool Search Tool, which lets Claude dynamically discover tools on-demand rather than loading all definitions upfront. This can reduce token usage by up to 85% while improving tool selection accuracy."}]}
{"id":"c38","kind":"numeric","text":"원문은 Claude Code 의 system prompt 를 80% 넘게 줄인 일에 skill 과 tool 을 progressive disclosure 로 바꾼 몫이 들어 있다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"This removes the main reason teams previously split work across subagents. In fact, we reduced Claude Code’s system prompt for more advanced models by over 80% which included cuts related to progressively disclosing skills and tools."}]}
{"id":"c39","kind":"absence","text":"20개 이상과 30-50개를 나란히 놓은 비교는 원문에 없다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§MCP tools","quote":"We recommend tools grouped by user intent (not one tool per API) because once you exceed 30-50 tool definitions in the system prompt, tool choice tends to degrade."}],"search":"grep -n -E '20\\+|15-20' .research/2026-10-26-fold-subagents-into-main-loop/notes/web/w1.txt  # 원문에는 30-50 만 있고 2026-01 글의 기준을 언급하지 않는다"}
{"id":"c40","kind":"web","text":"2024-12 글이 소개한 workflow 는 미리 정한 코드 경로로 모델과 tool 을 엮는다. routing 은 입력을 분류해 전문 prompt 와 tool 로 보내고, 예로 고객 지원 질의를 든다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w4.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w4","locator":"§What are agents?","quote":"Workflows are systems where LLMs and tools are orchestrated through predefined code paths."},{"source":"w4","locator":"§Workflow: Routing","quote":"Routing classifies an input and directs it to a specialized followup task. This workflow allows for separation of concerns, and building more specialized prompts."},{"source":"w4","locator":"§Workflow: Routing","quote":"Directing different types of customer service queries (general questions, refund requests, technical support) into different downstream processes, prompts, and tools."}]}
{"id":"c41","kind":"web","text":"원문에서 계획을 쓴 모델이 실행도 하므로 턴 중간에 계획을 고칠 수 있고, 원문은 이것을 orchestrator 구성과 가장 크게 다른 점으로 꼽는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"This is the main change from the orchestrator and specialist agents setup: the model that writes the plan is also the one carrying it out, so it can change the plan mid-turn."}]}
{"id":"c42","kind":"web","text":"원문은 순서와 domain 절차를 skill 로, 검증과 승인 gate 와 대화 중 memory 조회를 tool 로 옮긴다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"Ordering and domain procedure move into skills."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"Hard limits (validation, approval gates) and anything else that comes up mid-conversation (e.g. memory lookup) move into the tools."}]}
{"id":"c43","kind":"web","text":"원문은 payload 만들기, stream 파싱, 확인 질문 뒤 재개 같은 기계적인 부분과 값싸고 거의 늘 필요한 load 는 코드로 남겨도 된다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"Code can still be used to load anything cheap and almost always relevant (e.g. an entity resolution step), and to handle any mechanical parts (payload construction, stream parsing, resuming a clarification) inside tools the loop calls."}]}
{"id":"c44","kind":"web","text":"원문은 규칙 목록으로 계획을 다시 쓰는 코드 단계가 더는 필요 없다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"A code step that rewrites the plan from a catalog of rules is no longer needed, since the model decides each step."}]}
{"id":"c45","kind":"web","text":"Claude Code 도 처음에는 파일 삭제 같은 최악을 피하려 강한 규칙을 prompt 에 넣었다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w7.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w7","locator":"§Then: Give Claude rules / Now: Let Claude use judgement","quote":"When we first rolled out Claude Code, we needed to be sure that Claude avoided worst case scenarios, such as deleting files. This meant we would give particularly strong guidance that might not always be true."}]}
{"id":"c46","kind":"web","text":"tool 이 사용자별 권한을 확인하고 모델이 읽을 거절을 돌려주므로, 권한 수준마다 agent 를 따로 두지 않아도 한 loop 가 접근 범위가 다른 사용자를 받는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§MCP tools","quote":"Each tool checks what the calling user may see or do and returns a plain refusal the model can read, so one loop can serve users with different access without a separate agent per permission level."}]}
{"id":"c47","kind":"web","text":"원문은 새 모델이 나올 때마다 판단을 하네스에서 모델로 더 옮길 수 있고, 경직된 multi-agent 구조가 새 모델이 일을 더 맡는 것을 자주 막았다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"Each new model lets you move more of the decision-making out of the harness and into the model itself."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"A simpler loop is also easier to move to the next model; in migrations we have helped customers with, rigid multi-agent structures were often what stopped the new model from doing more of the work."}]}
{"id":"c48","kind":"web","text":"원문이 subagent 를 쓰라고 하는 조건은 context bloat 로 잴 만한 성능 저하, 버릴 새 context 로 하는 병렬 작업, tool 선택 실패나 system prompt 의 지시 충돌이다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"A single agent loop hits measurable performance degradation from context bloat, or"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"Multiple tasks need to be tackled in parallel with fresh context windows that can be discarded once the task is done, or"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"A single agent struggles to select appropriate tools or there are conflicting instructions in the system prompt."}]}
{"id":"c49","kind":"doc","text":"kit 은 호출당 수만 토큰을 읽으면 context 조건에 해당하고 수천 토큰이면 해당하지 않는다고 보고, tool 이 덜 돌려주게 할 수 있으면 fold 를 먼저 묻게 한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"anthropics/single-agent-loop-kit@c437962 기준","evidence":[{"source":"r1","locator":"skill/steps/00-audit.md:75","quote":"1. **Context.** It reads far more than the main agent needs afterwards: logs, long\n   documents, big search results. As a rough guide, tens of thousands of tokens per call\n   qualifies, and a few thousand does not."},{"source":"r1","locator":"skill/steps/00-audit.md:78","quote":"Before you settle on this, ask whether the tool\n   could simply return less (filter, search, paginate). If it could, the better plan is\n   often `fold` with a better tool."}]}
{"id":"c50","kind":"doc","text":"kit 의 병렬 조건은 여러 새 context 가 따로 탐색하거나 한 agent 가 다른 agent 의 작업을 과정을 보지 않고 검증하는 경우이고, tool 조건은 main agent 가 tool 을 잘못 고르는 것이 측정되거나 skill 로 풀리지 않는 지시 충돌이 있는 경우다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"anthropics/single-agent-loop-kit@c437962 기준","evidence":[{"source":"r1","locator":"skill/steps/00-audit.md:80","quote":"2. **Parallel or independent work.** Several fresh contexts explore separately for\n   thoroughness, or one checks another's work without seeing how it was produced."},{"source":"r1","locator":"skill/steps/00-audit.md:82","quote":"3. **Tool overload or conflict that skills cannot fix.** The main agent measurably picks\n   the wrong tools with everything loaded, or the instructions truly contradict each other."}]}
{"id":"c51","kind":"web","text":"문제 유형 대신 context 로 나누라는 원칙은 2026-01 글에 먼저 있었다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w2","locator":"§(분해 원칙)","quote":"The key insight is to adopt a context-centric view rather than a problem-centric view when decomposing work."},{"source":"w2","locator":"§(분해 원칙)","quote":"In one experiment with agents specialized by software development role (planner, implementer, tester, reviewer), the subagents spent more tokens on coordination than on actual work."}]}
{"id":"c52","kind":"web","text":"2025-06 글도 subagent 결과가 lead agent 를 거치며 줄어드는 일을 game of telephone 이라고 불렀다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w5.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w5","locator":"§Production reliability and engineering challenges","quote":"Subagent output to a filesystem to minimize the ‘game of telephone.’"}]}
{"id":"c53","kind":"web","text":"원문은 남긴 subagent 도 main agent 가 tool 로 부르게 하고, 대화를 넘기는 handoff 는 사용자와 직접 말해야 할 때만 쓰라고 권한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Subagents called as tools","quote":"We’d only recommend a full handoff, where the subagent takes over the conversation, when it needs to talk to the user directly. Everything else can be a skill plus tools in the main loop."}]}
{"id":"c54","kind":"web","text":"context 를 떼어 놓을 수 있는 대표적인 일은 독립된 조사 경로, 인터페이스가 깔끔한 별도 component, 블랙박스 검증이다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준, 2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w2.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"If you go the multi-agent route, start with the simplest pattern (generator-verifier, orchestrator-subagent, or other) that could work. Decompose boundaries effectively by dividing by context:"},{"source":"w2","locator":"§(분해 원칙)","quote":"The key insight is to adopt a context-centric view rather than a problem-centric view when decomposing work."}]}
{"id":"c55","kind":"web","text":"단일 loop 에서는 한 모델과 한 context window 가 tool loop 를 돌고, 턴과 비용 예산과 write gate 는 하네스가 정한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"One model and one context window running an open-ended tool loop, with limits (turn and cost budgets, write gates) set in the harness."}]}
{"id":"c56","kind":"web","text":"모델이 매 턴 tool call 묶음을 내면 하네스가 병렬로 돌려 가공하지 않은 결과를 같은 모델에 돌려주고, 모델이 다음 걸음으로 tool 묶음, 사용자에게 질문, 답 가운데 하나를 고른다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"Each turn, the model emits a batch of tool calls. The harness runs them in parallel and returns raw results to the same model, which decides the next step: another batch, a question to the user, or an answer."}]}
{"id":"c57","kind":"web","text":"loop 는 모델이 답하거나 예산에 닿으면 멈추고, 답 뒤에 goal 이나 verifier 검사를 붙일 수 있다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"The loop stops when the model answers or hits a budget. A goal or verifier check can optionally run after the answer."}]}
{"id":"c58","kind":"numeric","text":"그림 1 왼쪽은 orchestrator, intent classifier, 다섯 단계 pipeline, 사용자 구간 bucket, 추천 branch 의 다섯 층이고, 오른쪽은 system prompt 하나와 얇은 data tool 4-5개, 출력 guardrail 의 한 loop 다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"We also often see proposed agent designs that follow a familiar progression: an intent classifier, a fixed multi-step reasoning pipeline, user-segment buckets, separate recommendation branches, and a multi-agent orchestrator on top."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§(머리말)","quote":"In these cases feedback is often that most of this structure was doing work the model no longer needed done for it, and that one clear system prompt, 4-5 thin data tools, and firm output guardrails would cover most of the use case."}]}
{"id":"c59","kind":"code","text":"kit 의 reference_loop/loop.py 는 하네스 제한으로 턴 예산, subagent 가 쓴 토큰까지 세는 토큰 예산, 한 묶음의 호출 수 상한, 쓰기 tool 앞의 write gate 를 둔다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"anthropics/single-agent-loop-kit@c437962 기준","evidence":[{"source":"r1","locator":"reference_loop/loop.py:14","quote":"  * Hard limits live in the harness, not the prompt: a turn budget, a token\n    budget that also counts what subagents spend, a cap on calls per batch,\n    and a write gate in front of any tool that changes something."},{"source":"r1","locator":"reference_loop/loop.py:3","quote":"\"\"\"A small single agent loop, written to be read."}]}
{"id":"c60","kind":"web","text":"원문은 단일 loop 가 사용자의 큰 목표를 이해하고 대신 행동하는 agent 로 가는 데도 낫다고 적는다. agent 가 알게 된 것이 모두 한 context 에 남기 때문이다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop","quote":"This single loop design also helps with the end state many teams are working toward (an agent that understands a user's high-level goals and acts on their behalf), since it keeps everything the agent has learned in one context."}]}
{"id":"c61","kind":"numeric","text":"eval 은 중앙 팀의 end-to-end 세트와 skill 마다 딸린 작은 세트로 이뤄지고, golden example 10개로 시작할 수 있다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Task-completion evals","quote":"The eval structure we’ve seen work is one shared end-to-end set owned by a central team with smaller eval sets shipped with each skill by the team that owns it. Even a set of 10 golden examples is enough to start."}]}
{"id":"c62","kind":"web","text":"서로의 출력을 잇거나, 같은 데이터를 만지거나, 자주 함께 불리는 전문 agent 를 합친다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Combining domain agents","quote":"Merge specialists that chain on each other's output, touch the same data, or are often called together."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Combining domain agents","quote":"For example, if a significant share of production traffic is one specialist followed by a second, that is a tightly coupled pair, which makes it a candidate to merge into one domain agent."}]}
{"id":"c63","kind":"web","text":"남길 subagent 는 main agent 가 tool 로 부르고 공통 응답 schema 를 받으며, subagent 를 다시 쓰지 않아도 된다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Subagents called as tools","quote":"This will allow you to define a shared response schema for subagents, verify the conclusion against real data with the main agent, and trim the input to any final synthesis step. This is a good first step, as you don’t need to rewrite the subagents."}]}
{"id":"c64","kind":"web","text":"fold 는 subagent 의 prompt 를 skill 로, API 호출을 MCP tool 로 옮기고 subagent 가 있을 때와 없을 때를 비교한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Folding subagents into the main agent via skills and tools","quote":"Fold subagents into the main agent one at a time by turning each one’s prompts into skills and API calls into MCP tools. Compare eval performance with and without the subagent. Then decide which to keep."}]}
{"id":"c65","kind":"web","text":"합친 쪽이 더 나쁠 때만 그 subagent 를 남긴다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Tools to accelerate this work","quote":"Build a small end-to-end eval, fold in one subagent, and keep it as a subagent only if the folded version scores worse, then rinse and repeat."}]}
{"id":"c66","kind":"web","text":"원문은 함께 도는 agent 사슬마다 task 를 두고 task 마다 두 번 이상 돌리라고 한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Folding subagents into the main agent via skills and tools","quote":"Before each change, make sure your eval has a task for every chain of agents that runs together in production and for every rule the agent must not break, and run each task more than once, since a break like this one only showed up in one run out of two."}]}
{"id":"c67","kind":"web","text":"eval 은 처음에는 최종 답을 rubric 으로 채점하고, orchestrator 가 남은 동안은 routing 정확도를, 합친 뒤에는 맞는 skill 과 tool 을 골랐는지를 본다. 구조 비교에는 task 완료 eval 이 가장 중요하다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Task-completion evals","quote":"Grading the agent's final message against a rubric is a good starting point for tracking answer quality."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Task-completion evals","quote":"While you still have an orchestrator, you should also track routing accuracy (did it pick the right subagent?). Once a subagent is folded in, check instead whether the agent loaded the right skill or called the right tool."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Task-completion evals","quote":"Working toward task-completion evals over time is helpful as this matters most when comparing architectures."}]}
{"id":"c68","kind":"web","text":"내부 시스템을 replay 하기 어려우면 중요한 사건에 timestamp 를 남겨 뒤에 targeted eval 로 replay 하는 방법을 원문은 소개한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Task-completion evals","quote":"One approach that has worked for us internally is to record timestamps on important events, so they can be replayed later to run as targeted evals."}]}
{"id":"c69","kind":"web","text":"tool 로 부르는 단계에도 정보를 잃은 요약과 중첩 loop 의 지연이 남는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Subagents called as tools","quote":"Each call still hands back a lossy summary"},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Subagents called as tools","quote":"Every call is a nested model loop that adds latency"}]}
{"id":"c70","kind":"web","text":"원문은 sample support agent 에서 subagent 하나를 합치자 지연은 줄었지만 통과하던 과정이 깨졌다고 적는다. main agent 가 주문 조회 tool 을 쥐고 shipping 에게 배송일을 묻지 않고 혼자 답했다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Folding subagents into the main agent via skills and tools","quote":"When we tested this on a sample support agent, folding one subagent into another lowered latency, but also broke a process that had been passing. The main agent was holding the order lookup tool and answering on its own, without asking the shipping specialist for the delivery date."}]}
