{"id":"c88","kind":"doc","text":"고정된 단계만 있는 subagent 는 workflow 이므로 plain code 이고, 고정된 부분은 tool 안으로, 판단이 필요한 부분은 skill 로 가서 판정은 fold 다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"anthropics/single-agent-loop-kit@c437962 기준","evidence":[{"source":"r1","locator":"skill/steps/00-audit.md:91","quote":"- Its steps are fixed. Fixed steps are a workflow, which is plain code. Give it `fold`: the\n  fixed part goes inside a tool, and whatever still needs judgment (choosing, explaining)\n  goes in a skill."}]}
{"id":"c89","kind":"web","text":"원문은 팀들이 소유 단위를 agent 에서 skill 과 tool 로 옮기고, 작은 중앙 팀 하나가 system prompt 와 end-to-end 품질을 맡으며 새 tool 과 eval 을 내보내기 전에 검토하라고 한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§How several teams can contribute to a single agent","quote":"Individual teams can shift their ownership from agents to skills and tools, with one small central team keeping ownership of the system prompt and end-to-end quality."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Using an agent loop with progressive disclosure","quote":"One central team should own end-to-end quality and the system prompt, vetting every new tool and eval before it ships. Keeping that central team small helps iteration move quickly and lowers coordination cost across a large org."}]}
{"id":"c90","kind":"web","text":"MCP tool 은 행동, 실시간 데이터 읽기, 정해진 모양의 결과에 맞고, 이행 중에는 subagent 를 계속 부르는 통로로도 쓴다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§MCP tools","quote":"Tools are the right fit when the agent needs to take an action, read live data from a system, or return a result in a fixed shape. You can also use tools as a way to keep calling subagents while you migrate."}]}
{"id":"c91","kind":"web","text":"앞 tool 의 출력이 필요한 tool 은 그것이 있는지 스스로 확인하고 모델이 따를 지시를 돌려준다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§MCP tools","quote":"For example, if Y needs X's output, Y's tool checks for it and returns an instruction the model can act on."}]}
{"id":"c92","kind":"web","text":"skill 은 예전에 전문 subagent 의 prompt 가 담던 단계, 규칙, 판단에 맞고, 팀마다 DRI 가 자기 skill 을 eval 과 함께 내보낸다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Skills","quote":"Skills are the right fit when the agent needs to know how a team does work, like the steps, rules, and judgment calls a specialist subagent's prompt used to hold."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Skills","quote":"To prevent skill sprawl, you can have DRIs per team own their skills and make sure they are well crafted, distinct, and shipped with appropriate evals."}]}
{"id":"c93","kind":"web","text":"/skill-doctor 는 skill 마다 비용과 실제 사용 빈도를 보여 주고 안 쓰는 것을 지우게 한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Skills","quote":"/skill-doctor allows you to see what each skill in your library costs and how often it’s actually used, and delete dead weight."}]}
{"id":"c94","kind":"web","text":"knowledge base 는 가끔만 필요한 참고 자료에 맞고, 검색이나 조회 tool 뒤에 두거나 skill 의 참고 파일로 싣는다. 코드가 가져와 prompt 에 붙여 넣는 방식은 피한다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge bases","quote":"Knowledge bases are the right fit for reference material the agent only needs some of the time."},{"source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge bases","quote":"Facts and reference material (policies, metric definitions, product specs) can sit behind a search or lookup tool the model calls, or ship as reference files inside a skill. Avoid having code retrieve and paste this context into prompts."}]}
{"id":"c95","kind":"numeric","text":"2026-09 commerce 글은 트래픽의 1/3 이상에 걸리는 것은 system prompt 에 두고 나머지는 skill 에 두라는 출발점을 준다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w8.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w8","locator":"§Skills, not subagents","quote":"A good starting point is that anything relevant to a third or more of your traffic, whether anticipated before launch or observed in production, goes in the system prompt, and the rest goes in skills."}]}
{"id":"c96","kind":"web","text":"원문은 어느 구조든 그 뒤의 원칙만큼 중요하지 않다고 적는다. 재고, 한 번에 하나만 바꾸고, 버티는 것을 남기라는 원칙이다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Tools to accelerate this work","quote":"That makes any one architecture less important than the principle behind it: measure, change one thing at a time, and keep what holds up."}]}
{"id":"c97","kind":"web","text":"원문은 모델이 나아지고 agent 가 오래 돌수록 더 많은 subagent 가 skill 과 tool 이 될 수 있고, 한 번에 옮길 필요는 없다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Tools to accelerate this work","quote":"As models get more capable and agents get longer running, more of your subagents can be skills and tools. You don’t have to make that move in one step, though."}]}
{"id":"c98","kind":"web","text":"prompt-audit 은 prompt, skill, tool 설명에서 예전 모델에 맞춰 쓴 지시를 찾아 diff 로 고칠 안을 낸다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w1.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w1","locator":"§Tools to accelerate this work","quote":"/claude-api prompt-audit: can flag instructions written for older models in your prompts, skills, and tool descriptions and propose fixes as a diff."}]}
{"id":"c99","kind":"web","text":"2026-07 글은 규칙을 판단으로, 앞에 다 싣던 방식을 progressive disclosure 로 바꿨다고 적는다.","verdict":"confirmed","scope":"2026-10-25 수신 고정 사본(notes/web/w7.txt) 기준","evidence":[{"source":"w7","locator":"§Unhobbling Claude","quote":"And while these constraints were once needed to avoid worst case scenarios, we have since found we can delete many of them and let the model use surrounding context and judgement instead."},{"source":"w7","locator":"§Then: Put it all upfront / Now: Use progressive disclosure","quote":"Some of our tools are ‘deferred loading,’ which means the agent must search for their full definitions using ToolSearch before using them."}]}
